      "claim": "These regional cultures display characteristics of chiefdoms or early states (social hierarchy, elite burials, centralized production) before any political unification of China.",
      "evidence": "Findings such as elite tombs at Erlitou, large fortified towns at Shijiahe, and differentiated craft production demonstrate proto‑state organization.",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Consequently, the origins of Chinese civilization are best described as arising from multiple chiefdoms and early states spread throughout various Chinese regions, not from a single site.",
