      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Option (A) – the site of Anyang – refers to a late Shang capital (c. 1300–1046 BCE) that post‑dates the formative Neolithic cultures, so it cannot represent the origins of Chinese civilization.",
      "evidence": "Anyang (Yinxu) yields oracle‑bone script and royal tombs of the Shang dynasty, which are products of an already established civilization.",
